The complexity of the BF subproblem is primarily determined by the Monte Carlo sample size $M_t$ and the maximum number of iterations $I_{\max}$, resulting in a complexity of $O(I_{\max}M_t)$. The MA positioning subproblem incurs a higher complexity of $O(MI_{\max}M_t)$ due to the sequential exploration of positions for each of the $M$ antenna elements. Incorporating $I_{\max}$ outer-loop AO iterations, the overall algorithmic complexity is ultimately characterized as $O(I_{\max}(MI_{\max}M_t +I_{\max}M_t))$.
