\subsection{Communicating Finite-State Machines}

Communicating finite-state machines (CFMs) are the operational counterpart to HMSCs
and represent a low-level model of distributed systems. While HMSCs offer the possibility
to connect specific send and receive events, synchronization in CFMs is solely accomplished
via FIFO channels. 

