\begin{theorem}\label{thm:complexity}
Let $f\in \QQ [x]$ be an irreducible polynomial with Galois group $G,$ and let $\alpha $ be any root of $f$.
Then the complexity of $\alpha $ equals
\begin{itemize}
    \item[1.]  $\botn(G)$, relative to $\Calg $, and
    \item[2.] $\abot(G)$, relative to $\Cab $.
    \end{itemize}
