Since $\FF \subset \FF '
$, the Galois correspondence implies that $G\cong G'/N'$ for some normal subgroup of $N' \unlhd G'.$
Corresponding to~\eqref{eq:tower-F'}, are both the subgroup chain in $G'$ given by
\begin{equation}\label{eq:chain-G'}
G' = H_0 ' \supset \cdots \supset H_m ',
\end{equation}
as well as the subgroup chain in $G$ given by 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:chain-G}
G = H_0 \supset \cdots \supset H_m  ,
