Moreover, the reverse inequality must hold for any maximal subgroup $M$ which appears in a chain attaining the minimum Galois width $\botn (G).$
Such an $M$ is clearly a (maximal) subgroup of minimum index in $G$.
Thus, using~\Cref{prop:simple-perm-degree}, $$\botn(G) = [G:M]=\mu (G).$$
