In the following, we consider two cases. First, we prove Theorem \ref{theorem:geometric-interpolation-equivalent-Gaussian-Hilbert-space}  for the case $S_i \in \SymTr(\Hcal)_{< I}$, $i=0,1$.
Then we proceed to the general case $S_i \in \SymHS(\Hcal)_{< I}$, $i=0,1$, via a limiting process.
We need the following technical results. The first is a result on Gaussian integrals on $\Hcal$ from \cite{DaPrato:PDEHilbert}.

