Since $S_0, S_1 \in \SymTr(\Hcal)_{<I}$, we have $A \in \Sym(\Hcal) \cap \Tr(\Hcal)$. Furthermore,
\begin{align*}
I - A = (1-\alpha)(I-S_0)^{-1} + \alpha (I-S_1)^{-1} > 0.
\end{align*}
Thus $A \in \SymTr(\Hcal)_{< I}$.
By Proposition \ref{proposition:exponetial-quadratic-whitenoise-Gaussian},
\begin{align}
