Our simulations show that this modulated inhibition is necessary to properly encode (train) patterns with varying coding-level. We look into whether this coding-level-dependent inhibition is relevant beyond training by testing \glspl{sfnn} with and without it during inference. Similarly to the previous simulations, each data point measures the average mean rate response to the same $N_{ts} = 20$ ($10$ samples per class) testing samples for 10 independently trained and tested \glspl{sfnn} on both settings.

