Limitations of static prompts without explicit output schema are evident in cases with atypical key phrases or headers. Cases discussed in figure \ref{fig:schema} highlights the importance of including output schema in the extraction prompts. Extraction accuracy is influenced not just by page count and scan quality, but also by document formatting. Multi-line headers and dark-shaded key phrases often reduce accuracy, mainly due to issues in text conversion rather than LLM behavior. Processing documents as images generally yields more reliable results than pre-converting them to text.


