We evaluated fuzzers' performance using various security vulnerabilities in C programs. Specifically, we adopted the 41 vulnerabilities from DAFL \cite{kim_dafl_2023}, detailed in Table \ref{tab:vuls}.
As is common in vulnerability-exposing fuzzing efforts, we built all target binaries with ASAN (AddressSanitizer). But since Beacon doesn't support fuzzing ASAN-compiled target binaries, we ran an extra experiment without ASAN to compare with Beacon.

