    (b) An optimal conforming partition of $ P _ 1 $ with stabbing number~$ 4 $. %
    (c) The pixelation of a polygon $ P _ 1 $ in general position 
    with one hole. 
    The reflex vertices are tiny (black) discs and the reflex segments are dotted (red). The horizontal and vertical reflex segments $ \mathbf { h } _ p $ and $ \mathbf { v } _ p $ from the reflex vertex $ p $ are bold. The wedge-pixel of $ p $ is shaded (in orange) and labeled~$ 1 $.%
    (d) The pixelation of a thin polygon $ P _ 2 $ with three holes (not in general position).
    (e) An optimal conforming partition of $ P _ 2 $ with stabbing number~$ 3 $.
