In this section, we detail the experiments conducted to compare our proposal against the encoding presented in \cite{fischetti}. Our evaluation consists of two main experiments. In the first one, we compare the two encodings using $12$ datasets. In the second one, we conduct a detailed comparison using a single dataset. We vary the architecture of the trained ANNs to explore the effect of the number of layers and neurons. We evaluate the performance of each encoding in terms of time for building logical constraints and time for computing explanations. We explained all instances in a given dataset and calculated the average time and standard deviation to compare times for computing explanations. In the other case, given a trained ANN on a dataset, we built the logical constraints $10$ times and calculated the average time and standard deviation. 

