\noindent\textbf{Noise Multiplier Calculation.} 
\phantomsection  
\label{noise}
To implement DP adaptively, noise levels are dynamically adjusted based on client compliance scores. The noise multiplier (\(N_m\)) is computed as: $N_m = (1.0 - S_c) + \text{Min Noise Multiplier}$, where \( S_c \) denotes the client's compliance score, and \(\text{Min Noise Multiplier}\) (set to \(1e\text{-}10\) in this experiment) ensures baseline privacy. This approach ensures that clients with lower compliance scores need higher noise levels. Noise can be tuned or clipped per FL aggregation strategy, protecting data while preserving model quality and ensuring secure FL participation.

